/api/games/me should return all needed info for an active player's current turn. this includes
- the game id
- the game name
- the total number of turns in this game
- the current game turn
- the current turn game piece
- this player's active game board at the start of the turn
- this player's current turn
- the time remaining until the next turn

If the game has not started (current time before start time), then the turn number 
is -1, the current turn game piece is empty, and the active game board is all spaces.

The frontend will not send the player's move until the start of the next turn. When
the backend receive's the player's move, it will compute the new game board, score it
and remove scored blocks, then indicate success. at that point, the next call to 
/api/games/me will return the game state for the next turn.

The move for turn N must be sent during turn N+1.

POST to /api/games/move/id should only return success if the move was legal and
error if the move was not legal. The caller is expected to get an update from 
/api/games/me shortly thereafter for the player to choose the next move.

